              "text": "common flexor-pronator wad muscles of medial epicondyle include",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "pronator teres",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "flexor carpi radialis",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "palmaris longus",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "flexor digitorum superficialis",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "flexor carpi ulnaris",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Blood supply",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "anterior",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "branches of **inferior ulnar collateral artery**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "posterior",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "branches of the **superior and inferior ulnar collateral artery**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Classification",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "No routinely used classification system",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Can be more simply classified as **acute** vs. **chronic**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "acute subtypes",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "Nondisplaced",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "Minimally displaced",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "Displaced",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "Fragment entrapped in joint",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "Fracture through epicondyle apophysis",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "chronic",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "related to **tension stress injuries**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "medial elbow pain",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "valgus instability",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "ecchymosis (especially with direct trauma)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "ulnar nerve dysfunction- motor and sensory function should be documented in all cases",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "generalize swelling suggests elbow may have dislocated",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiographs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "displacement is difficult to measure accurately as medial epicondyle is located on the posteromedial aspect of the distal humerus and fragment displaces anteriorly",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "recommended views",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "AP and lateral of elbow",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "internal oblique view to evaluate displacement",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**distal humeral axial view**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "may also improve accuracy of measuring displacement",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [
                        {
                          "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4008/images/illus_b.jpg",
                          "caption": "Illustration demonstrating the different radiographs, including oblique radiographs, for accurate assessment of medial epicondyle fractures"
                        },
                        {
                          "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4008/images/illus_a_.jpg",
                          "caption": "Picture demonstrating the technique to obtain a distal humeral axial view"
                        }
                      ],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "obtained by angling beam **25 degrees anterior to long axis of humerus**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "CT",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "most accurate but associated with increased radiation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4008/images/illus_c.jpg",
                  "caption": "3D CT scan of medial epicondyle fracture"
                }
              ],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Differential",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Medial condyle** fracture",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Simple elbow dislocation",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Nonoperative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "immobilization (1-3 weeks) in a long arm cast with elbow flexed to 90 degrees",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "controversial",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "historically <5mm displacement",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "displacement >2mm without upper limit may be tolerated, as RCTs included mean displacement ~7mm with equivalent outcomes to surgery",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "amount of true displacement difficult to determine on plain radiographs",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "no fragment incarceration in the elbow joint",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "elbow reduced if associated dislocation present",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "outcomes",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "functional outcomes equivalent to surgical treatment regardless of displacement amount",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "lower rate of osseous union rate compared to surgically treated patients",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "radiographic nonunion (or fibrous union) often asymptomatic",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "despite high rates of nonunion with non-operative treatment, radiological union shows poor correlation with functional outcomes",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "grip strength and range of motion equalize by 3 months",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Operative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "open reduction internal fixation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "absolute",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "displaced fx with **entrapment of medial epicondyle fragment in joint**",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [
                            {
                              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4008/images/Dislocation%20with%20entrapment%20of%20medial%20epicondyle_moved.gif",
                              "caption": "AP and lateral radiographs showing entrapment of medial epicondyle fragment in the joint"
                            }
                          ],
                          "importance": "5",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "extension to the articular surface with **medial condyle** involvement (articular surface)",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "4",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "open fracture",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "relative",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "**ulnar nerve dysfunction**",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "4",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "**> 2-15mm displacement, also controversial**",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "4",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "**>2-5 mm in valgus stress athletes such as throwers or gymnasts**",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "5",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "associated elbow dislocation",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Techniques",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Open Reduction Internal Fixation**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "approach",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**medial approach to elbow**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "typically with patient supine and arm abducted to 90 degrees, a prone position also described",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "incision is made directly over medial epicondyle",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "brachialis/triceps interval",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "ulnar nerve at risk",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "technique",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "identify and protect ulnar nerve (easiest from proximal to distal)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "reduce fracture",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "screw fixation (often cannulated)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4008/images/ap.jpg",
                      "caption": ""
                    },
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4008/images/lat.jpg",
                      "caption": ""
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "a washer may improve fixation, but more prominant",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "avoid iatrogenic comminution during screw insertion",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "K-wires indicated for smaller fragments or in younger children",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Complications",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Non-union**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**majority are asymptomatic**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "odds of radiographic union are 9 times greater with surgery",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Nerve injury**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "ulnar nerve (reported between 10% - 16%)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "neuropraxia after dislocation will usually resolve with observation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "radial nerve at risk with bicortical screw fixation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Missed incarceration in elbow joint**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "consider in younger patients without ossification of medial epicondyle",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Elbow stiffness**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "the most common complication is the loss of few degrees of elbow extension",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "associated with prolonged immobilization, occurs after nonoperative and operative treatment",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Prognosis",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Good to excellent results** have been reported for both surgical and non-surgical management",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    }
